>
  <h2>Sourcing and provenance</h2>
  <p>Technical claims should cite an appropriate source and preserve enough context to understand what the source actually supports. A manufacturer specification, third-party publication, direct observation, and editorial inference are different evidence categories and should not be presented as interchangeable.</p>

  <h2>Evidence versus interpretation</h2>
  <p>HydroRigor should identify where a conclusion depends on editorial judgment. Uncertainty, conflicting evidence, or missing information should be stated instead of concealed behind false precision.</p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>Material factual errors should be corrected promptly once verified. Corrections can be sent through the contact page, and significant corrections should be noted where they could change a reader's decision.</p>

  <h2>Updates</h2>
  <p>Published dates and meaningful update dates should be visible. An update must not imply that every source, product, or recommendation was retested unless that work actually occurred.</p>

  <h2>Responsible AI assistance</h2>
  <p>AI tools may assist with structure, editing, code, consistency checks, or research organization. They do not create evidence, personal experience, product testing, or authority. Claims and citations remain subject to editorial verification.</p>

  <h2>Commercial independence</h2>
  <p>Compensation must be disclosed and must not determine the conclusion. M05 enforces typed commercial records, evidence boundaries, destination relationships, and separate acquisition disclosures. No affiliate destination or active compensated relationship is currently configured.</p>
</InfoPageLayout>
